# Page Builder Editor Responsive Controls

## Context
The section Appearance popover still renders raw HTML selects, so the global
select chevron and browser/theme indicator overlap in dark mode. The rich-text
editor also inherits app-wide button padding on TipTap's fixed-size drag controls
and TipTap's desktop `32px 80px` content padding at mobile widths, hiding the
modify icons and compressing editable text into a narrow centered column.

## Goal
- Use the shared `Select` primitive for section Appearance choices without
  breaking popover focus, outside-click, or nested menu interaction.
- Keep TipTap's add/modify controls visible and usable at desktop widths.
- Hide block modification controls and use renderer-like content padding on
  mobile so editable text uses the available width.

## Non-Goals
- Replacing TipTap, changing stored rich-text HTML, or redesigning its toolbar.
- Completing the broader raw-control migration tracked by
  `.todo/ui_primitive_consolidation`.
- Changing section-shell persistence or rendering contracts.

## Steps
1. Replace raw Appearance selects with the shared `Select` primitive and make
   the body-portaled Appearance panel cooperate with its body-portaled menus.
2. Scope desktop drag-control button resets to the editable TipTap wrapper.
3. Add mobile editor padding and drag-control visibility rules matching the
   renderer's responsive content behavior.
4. Add focused Appearance interaction regressions and run frontend verification.

## Verification
- Run the focused `SectionShellControls` test.
- Run frontend TypeScript/build and lint checks.
- Run `git diff --check` and confirm no raw select remains in
  `SectionShellControls.tsx`.

